**Lemma 3.3 (geometric inverse).** On the exact incidence layout of
Definition 2.5, S masks and B contours separately recover the entire raw
record $W$; re-encoding is the identity on their image. The masks have
$2V$ bits and the contour $4(V-1)+2L$ bits for actual vertex and terminal
counts $V,L$.

Proof. Use CYCLE Lemma 3.6 and UAS Theorem 3.2. Unary sockets distinguish
left0, right1 and absent, including at terminal scaffold sockets.
Terminal paths recover the finite prefix tree by prefix closure, and
the fixed component decomposition recovers tapes/tracks/finite slots.
Their proofs depend on $q$ only as a finite scaffold parameter, so apply
with $q_{\mathrm{gc}}$. No task or acquired-binding assertion is used. ∎

